 CODE
Art. 2.3.83. 
Acts to be registered
 The following are registered in the central register of matrimonial property agreements: 
1¡ matrimonial property agreements, whether concluded before or during the marriage; 
2¡ declarations of advance contribution contained in a deed of acquisition of ownership of immovable property in accordance with Article 2.3.53, ¤ 2; 
3¡ the agreements referred to in article 1478 of the former Civil Code; 
4¡ applications for separation as to property, and judgments and rulings pronouncing judicial separation as referred to in article 2.3.78; 
5¡ judgments and rulings pronouncing the withdrawal of the power of management of a married person or revoking such withdrawal, within the meaning of Article 2.3.40, ¤ 2; 
6¡ judgments and rulings pronouncing on the validity, application or interpretation of a matrimonial agreement.
The notary registers the deeds referred to in paragraph 1, 1¡ to 3¡.
 The clerk of the court with which they have been lodged communicates to the central register of matrimonial agreements the applications for separation of property referred to in paragraph 1, 4¡, as soon as they are placed on the roll.
 The registrar of the court that pronounced the judgments or rulings referred to in paragraph 1, 4¡, 5¡ and 6¡ shall communicate them to the central register of matrimonial property agreements.
 The registrar of the court which handed down the judgment or ruling referred to in paragraph 1, 4¡, communicates to the central register of matrimonial property agreements the oppositions, appeals or appeals lodged against the said judgment or ruling.
 The registrar of the court that pronounced the judgment or ruling shall notify the central register of matrimonial property agreements of judicial decisions annulling or reversing a judgment or ruling referred to in paragraph 1, 4¡, 5¡ and 6¡.
